<p>Smoke damage claims in McAllen often follow kitchen fires, electrical fires, garage fires, or a fire at a neighboring home or business. Smoke can contaminate an entire building through open doors, wall cavities, attic space, and especially the HVAC system, which in a hot Rio Grande Valley climate is running most of the year. The damage is not always obvious, and that makes smoke claims prone to disagreement.</p>
<p>Smoke damage can also come from outside your property. A fire in a neighboring unit, an adjacent business in a shared strip center, or a nearby structure can push smoke into your building even when no flames ever reached it. Those losses are still documented and claimed under your own policy, subject to its terms.</p>
<p>This page explains how smoke claims work. If your loss involves burned structure, see our <a href="/services/fire-damage-claims/">fire damage claims</a> page as well.</p>

<h2>Types of Smoke Damage Covered</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Soot deposits</strong> on walls, ceilings, cabinets, windows, and flooring.</li>
<li><strong>Odor</strong> absorbed into drywall, insulation, carpet, upholstery, and clothing.</li>
